@@ -281,6 +281,14 @@ Confirmed Host exit without successful task teardown displays localized recovery
 
 <a id="local-desktop-settings"></a>
 
+### Local source updates
+
+Local builds carrying `dshSourceUpdater: true` use the installed `%LOCALAPPDATA%/DSH Source Updater/updater-config.json` helper configuration. The helper runs under an independent Node executable outside the application installation. Cold and second launches check published official `dsh-v*` releases, including prereleases; concurrent launches share one build and no periodic release polling runs.
+
+The helper builds a fixed release commit with the saved source patch and plugin compatibility checks. An incompatible patch or plugin retains the current installation and opens a warning. The application menu's Source Update Status command displays the current result and offers Retry. Missing helper files leave ordinary application startup available.
+
+Installation requires saved drafts, sixty seconds without application input, and no running tasks, approval waits, queued messages or background jobs. The Host drains admitted requests and stops gracefully before the helper snapshots the application, Harness home and Electron data. Qualification runs against isolated data with schedules and user admission disabled; matching program and data snapshots remain available for rollback. Packaged mandatory-update policy remains active independently of this local source-update path.
+
 ### Local desktop settings
 
 The [shell configuration decision](../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-10-08-desktop-shell-configuration.md) defines Host-independent ownership and the criteria for evaluating existing settings for migration.
